  <div>
    {% set heading = "Resolver privacy and logging" %}{% set desc = "" %}
    {% include "section-heading.njk" %}

    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <p>DNS queries sent to the AEGIS PDNS resolver are processed by SecretChip infrastructure. Resolver operation may involve technical logs that include source IP address, timestamp, queried domain, query type, resolver endpoint used, policy decision, response code, and security or abuse metadata.</p>
      <p>Logs are used for service operation, abuse prevention, debugging, security monitoring, and improving filtering quality. <strong>SecretChip does not sell DNS query data.</strong></p>
      <p>Filtering is best-effort and may produce false positives or false negatives. Reports for false positives, false negatives, abuse, and privacy questions can be submitted via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      <p class="mini" style="margin-top: 10px;">Logs are retained only for as long as necessary for service operation, security, abuse prevention, troubleshooting, and legal obligations. See the <a href="/legal/privacy-notice/">Privacy Notice</a> for the complete data-handling description.</p>
    </div>
